<h2>Sizing a transformer: the 80% rule</h2>
<p class="lead">A low-voltage transformer should not run at its full rating. Loading it to about 80% leaves headroom for heat, start-up current and future fixtures, and helps it last.</p>
<p>Add up the wattage (or VA, if your LED fixtures list it) of every fixture, divide by 0.8, then choose the next standard size up. A 120 W load needs at least 150 W of capacity; a 250 W load needs at least about 313 W, so a 600 W unit gives room to grow, while a 300 W unit would be overloaded.</p>
<h2>Why voltage drop matters</h2>
<p>Wire has resistance. The longer the run and the more current it carries, the more voltage is lost before it reaches the fixtures. Halogen lamps showed this as dim, yellow light at the end of a run. Many LEDs tolerate a wider voltage range, but too little voltage can still cause flicker, dimming or shortened life.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Wire</th><th>Approx. ohms per 1,000 ft (per conductor)</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>16/2</td><td>4.02</td><td>Short leads to individual fixtures</td></tr>
<tr><td>14/2</td><td>2.53</td><td>Light loads, short runs</td></tr>
<tr><td>12/2</td><td>1.59</td><td>The workhorse for most home runs</td></tr>
<tr><td>10/2</td><td>1.00</td><td>Long or heavily loaded runs</td></tr>
<tr><td>8/2</td><td>0.63</td><td>Very long runs to distant zones</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>The calculator uses the worst case: all the load at the far end of the run. Spreading fixtures along the run, using a hub layout or a T-method connection reduces real-world drop. Multi-tap transformers (12, 13, 14, 15 V) let an installer push a little extra voltage down longer runs.</p>
<div class="callout callout--warn"><strong>Safety first:</strong> the transformer plugs into or is wired to 120 V household power. It should be mounted on an outdoor-rated GFCI-protected circuit with an in-use cover. Leave line-voltage work to a qualified professional.</div>
<p>Read the full guide: <a href="/landscape-lighting-transformer-sizing/">How to size a landscape lighting transformer</a>. If your lights are dim at the end of a run, our <a href="/services/landscape-lighting-repair/">repair service</a> can diagnose it.</p>
